# Ghidra project databases are committed, but they are not text.
#
# A .rep is a mix of binary (the HSQLDB pages, *.gbf) and XML (project.prp and
# the idata/*.prp property files). Without -merge, git is happy to text-merge
# two branches' project.prp on a two-branch merge and produce a project that is
# neither branch's -- a conflict-free merge that silently loses whichever side
# lost. -merge makes git refuse instead, which is the correct outcome: a
# project that two branches both rebuilt has to be re-rebuilt, not merged.
#
# This is not optional decoration; it is the difference between a loud conflict
# and a corrupt database.
*.gpr            binary -diff -merge
*.gbf            binary -diff -merge
**/*.rep/**      binary -diff -merge
